 ## Discord ops alerts
 
@@ -67,8 +67,11 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 | Item | Detail |
 | --- | --- |
 | Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
+| Mention (optional) | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` → `config('services.discord.mention_id')`; a Discord user ID of 17–20 digits, sent as `<@ID>` on its own line at the end of every alert |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
+| Unconfigured mention | Empty/invalid ID → no mention; anything that is not 17–20 ASCII digits (e.g. `@everyone`, `@here`, short IDs, newline injection) is silently ignored |
+| Limits | Whole content (including the mention) is capped at 1800 characters; when truncating, room for the mention is reserved so the ping always survives |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
 Call from jobs/handlers when a notable ops event occurs; do not wire every exception globally.
